  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 107 PM MDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nHot weather will continue Monday, although it may be a degree or two \ncooler across the plains. Readings of 104 to 108 will be likely from \nPueblo to the KS border along the US50 corridor. \n\nShowers and storms will continue in the higher terrain Monday \nwith the best chances along the CONTDVD. With flow becoming a \nbit more westerly aloft, there will be a better chance for some \nevening storms over the plains.\n\nFor Tuesday onward, temperatures will cool down a few degrees over \nthe plains with mainly 90s across the plains (although the \nLamar area will continue to be around 100). Showers and \nthunderstorms will continue over the mountains, and we will see \na bit better chance .of storms over the plains, especially on \nTuesday, as a weak boundary may push through on this day. \n\\/Hodanish",
